Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: guard NSS multicast aggregation state

The NSS Ethernet TX path permits a NULL station for multicast frames.
Only inspect per-station aggregation state when a station exists; multicast
has no per-station BA session. Leave the Ethernet offload path intact.

On WF810DF, starting secured APs triggers IPv6 MLD traffic before any client
exists. The embedded module's instruction at 0x3ebbc dereferences NULL sta
in ieee80211_8023_xmit(), reported after the nearest retained symbol as
__ieee80211_subif_start_xmit+0x49c. This causes a fatal exception in mld_ifc_work.

--- a/net/mac80211/tx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/tx.c
@@ -4774,7 +4774,7 @@ static void ieee80211_8023_xmit(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata,
 	ieee80211_aggr_check(sdata, sta, skb);

 	tid = skb->priority & IEEE80211_QOS_CTL_TAG1D_MASK;
-	tid_tx = rcu_dereference(sta->ampdu_mlme.tid_tx[tid]);
+	tid_tx = sta ? rcu_dereference(sta->ampdu_mlme.tid_tx[tid]) : NULL;
 	if (tid_tx) {
 		if (!test_bit(HT_AGG_STATE_OPERATIONAL, &tid_tx->state)) {
 			/* fall back to non-offload slow path */
